{"units":[
{"id":"tsdb/compact_test.go:BenchmarkFilterSeriesAndSortPostings","summary":"Adds a benchmark of Head.filterSeriesAndSortPostings at several input fractions. It runs only under go test -bench and does not touch production code.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"New benchmark for filterSeriesAndSortPostings at varying selectivity","confidence":0.95,"reason":"New benchmark-only code that cannot affect production behavior.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/db.go:var compactHeadViewBeforeEvictTestingCallback","summary":"Adds a package-level test hook variable that compactHeadViewLocked calls before eviction. It is nil in production, so it has no effect unless a test sets it.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Add testing callback hook invoked before head eviction","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Unexported hook that is nil unless a test sets it; the call site is reviewed in compactHeadViewLocked.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/db.go:(*DB).compactHeadViewLocked","summary":"Extracts the block-write, reload and evict loop shared by CompactStaleHead and CompactSelectedSeries. It adds an appendID watermark captured before writing, a loop bound that is now inclusive (mint <= maxt), skipping empty writes, and a pre-evict test hook. These change which series are evicted and which blocks are written, so a reviewer must judge them.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Shared head-view compaction helper with append-ID watermark and inclusive range","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Persistence and eviction logic with concurrency-sensitive watermark; data loss is possible if wrong.","risk_signals":["persistence","concurrency","data eviction","loop bound changed","error handling"],"focus":["maxt is read before the watermark is captured; check that a sample committed between the two reads, with a timestamp past the last written chunk range, is still protected by the evictor's maxt check","The empty-uids continue skips reloadBlocks; check that no state is left inconsistent","The package-global test callback is cleared after use and is not safe if compactions run concurrently","The inclusive loop bound writes an extra slice when maxt falls exactly on a chunk boundary"]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).selectedSeriesIndex","summary":"Renames staleIndex to selectedSeriesIndex and changes its argument and return types to the renamed types. The logic is unchanged.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","headline":"Rename staleIndex to selectedSeriesIndex","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Pure rename of an unexported method and types, with the caller (SelectedSeriesHead.Index) updated; the body is identical.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:type headSelectedSeriesIndexReader","summary":"Renames headStaleIndexReader to headSelectedSeriesIndexReader, renames its field, and rewrites the doc comment. The struct layout is otherwise the same and the type is unexported.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","headline":"Rename headStaleIndexReader to headSelectedSeriesIndexReader","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Rename of an unexported type and field with all uses updated in the PR; no logic change.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:type seriesRefs","summary":"Renames the unexported staleSeriesRefs struct to seriesRefs. The fields are unchanged.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","headline":"Rename staleSeriesRefs to seriesRefs","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Pure rename of an unexported struct with identical fields and all uses updated in the PR.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).filterSeriesAndSortPostings","summary":"Generalizes the stale-series lookup into a function that takes arbitrary postings and a keep predicate run under the series lock. Series are returned sorted by ref order and by labels. The stale and OOO logic moves into predicates, and the debug log text changes.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"Generalize stale series filtering to postings plus keep predicate","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Core series selection for compaction and eviction; the predicate and locking semantics determine which series are evicted.","risk_signals":["locking","data eviction","input ordering assumption"],"focus":["The predicate runs under s.Lock; check that no predicate takes other locks","sortedByRef follows the input order, so callers must pass ref-sorted postings (CompactSelectedSeries sorts and dedups)","When keep is nil, the series fields are not read under the lock; check that no caller passes nil"]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData","summary":"Reimplements staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData as a call to filterSeriesAndSortPostings with a predicate of no OOO data and stale. The predicate matches the removed inline logic.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData delegates to shared filter function","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Refactor with the same predicate (ooo == nil and stale NaN checks) as the removed inline code.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]}
]}

{"units":[
{"id":"tsdb/block.go:(*BlockMetaCompaction).SetSelectedSeries","summary":"Adds a method that appends the from-selected-series hint to block meta if absent and keeps hints sorted. It changes the persisted meta.json hints for selected-series blocks.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add SetSelectedSeries to record from-selected-series compaction hint","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Writes a new value into the persisted block meta Hints list, which other code uses for compaction and WAL cutoff decisions.","risk_signals":["persisted block meta format","new hint value"],"focus":["Hint is idempotent and sorted, so meta.json stays stable across repeated sets","Older Prometheus versions tolerate the unknown hint string when reading meta.json"]},
{"id":"tsdb/block.go:(*BlockMetaCompaction).FromSelectedSeries","summary":"Adds a read-only predicate reporting whether the from-selected-series hint is present. It is used by the planner, meta merge and inOrderBlocksMaxTime.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add FromSelectedSeries hint predicate","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Pure side-effect-free lookup; the behavior that depends on it is in the callers reviewed separately.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/block_test.go:TestBlockMetaCompaction_SetSelectedSeries","summary":"New unit test covering the selected-series hint: initially absent, set, idempotent, and independent of the stale hint. Test-only.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Test selected-series hint set/idempotence/independence","confidence":0.95,"reason":"New test only; cannot affect production behavior.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:(*LeveledCompactor).plan","summary":"The planner now splits blocks into stale, selected and no-hint classes and plans one class at a time, preferring no-hint, then stale, then selected. This keeps partial-view blocks from being merged with other classes, so the hint survives and the WAL-replay cutoff is not advanced.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Compaction planner segregates selected-series blocks from other block classes","confidence":0.92,"reason":"Changes which blocks get compacted together, which affects on-disk layout, compaction starvation and WAL-replay data safety.","risk_signals":["compaction planning logic","data-loss path (WAL cutoff)","possible starvation of partial-view classes"],"focus":["Only one class is planned per call, so stale or selected blocks wait until no-hint planning returns nothing","Overlapping blocks of different classes are never merged and are retained until retention","Behavior is unchanged when only one class exists"]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:(*LeveledCompactor).planClass","summary":"Comment-only update to the planClass doc describing the new partial-view classes.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"docs","headline":"Update planClass doc comment for selected-series hint","confidence":0.97,"reason":"Only comment lines changed; no code statements differ.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:CompactBlockMetas","summary":"When merging block metas, the from-selected-series hint is now propagated to the merged block if any source carries it, like the stale hint. Comments are updated accordingly.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Merged block metas now keep the from-selected-series hint","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Changes the persisted compaction hints of merged blocks, which feeds inOrderBlocksMaxTime and WAL truncation.","risk_signals":["persisted block meta","WAL-replay cutoff"],"focus":["Any-source propagation is correct only because the planner segregates classes; check other callers of CompactBlockMetas","Blocks with both stale and selected hints get both"]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:(*LeveledCompactor).Write","summary":"Write now copies the from-selected-series hint from the base block meta to the newly written block, mirroring the stale hint.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Write propagates from-selected-series hint from base meta","confidence":0.88,"reason":"Changes the hints persisted on newly written blocks, which affect WAL cutoff computation.","risk_signals":["persisted block meta"],"focus":["Callers passing a base meta get the hint set on the output block as intended"]},
{"id":"tsdb/db_test.go:TestCompactSelectedSeries","summary":"New happy-path test for CompactSelectedSeries: selected series are evicted, others stay, the block has the hint, HeadMinTime is unchanged, and metrics are updated. Part of the moved test code.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Add happy-path test for CompactSelectedSeries","confidence":0.93,"reason":"New test only; no production behavior change.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]}
]}
